624:| readme-map | gate | `node scripts/readme-map.mjs [--registry <path>] [--readme <path>] [--corpus <dir>]...` → `README_MAP: CLEAN` exit 0 / `DRIFT` exit 1 / `FAIL-CLOSED` exit 2 / usage 64, contract `kumitate-readme-map-v2` (round 58: every `covered` member must lstat as a regular file — a directory member is DRIFT `covered-not-file`, a dangling symlink DRIFT `stale-covered`; registry version 2); default `.ufo/pins/readme-map.json` pins the `covered` set — every `*.md` under `corpus/knowledge` + `corpus/lessons` must carry exactly one README map row `| `path` |`, every such row must name a live file, and every live file must be pinned; findings `uncovered`, `orphan-row`, `duplicate-row`, `format-unmapped`, `stale-covered`, `unpinned` are DRIFT; malformed registry/README/corpus-dir is FAIL-CLOSED | `--selftest` (16 hermetic cases; `README_MAP_SELFTEST: PASS (16/16)` + `VERDICT: PASS`) | `.ufo/pins/readme-map.json`; `corpus/README.md`; `pin.readme-map` in `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` |
625:| cite-sources | gate | `node scripts/cite-sources.mjs [--readme PATH] [--sources PATH]` → `CITE_SOURCES: CLEAN\|DRIFT\|FAIL-CLOSED` (0 clean · 1 a README map row cites an `S` + 3-or-more-digit id that is not a SOURCES row · 2 unreadable input · 64 usage), contract `kumitate-cite-sources-v1`; one- and two-digit family ids are ignored | `--selftest` (8 hermetic cases; `CITE_SOURCES_SELFTEST: PASS (8/8)` + `VERDICT: PASS`) | `pin.cite-sources` in `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` |
626:| dispatch-evidence | gate | `node scripts/dispatch-evidence.mjs --root DIR --round N --wave NAME [--expect planned=N,sessions=N,exit0=N,reports=N]` → `DISPATCH_EVIDENCE: CLEAN (seats=… sessions=… exit0=… reports=… dead=…)` (0 clean · 1 a real defect · 2 fail-closed · 64 usage), contract `kumitate-dispatch-evidence-v1` (round 60): reads the round's **actual** dispatch record — the launcher progress file `launcher-progress.tsv` and the sibling summary `dispatch-actual.json` — plus the seat report files; a registry whose members carry no session id is DRIFT `NOT_A_DISPATCH` (a prepared spec is not a dispatch); a dead seat (exit ≠ 0, no session id) is named and never credited (`DEAD_SEAT_UNCREDITED`, `DEAD_MISMATCH`); other findings `PLAN_MISMATCH`, `SESSION_MISMATCH`, `REPORT_ABSENT`, `REGISTRY_MISMATCH`, `EXPECT_MISMATCH`; fail-closed ids `PROGRESS_ABSENT`, `REGISTRY_UNREADABLE`, `WAVE_DIR_ABSENT` | `--selftest` (8 hermetic cases in `mkdtemp` fixtures; `DISPATCH_EVIDENCE_SELFTEST: PASS (8/8)` + `VERDICT: PASS`) | the round's committed `launcher-progress.tsv` / `dispatch-actual.json` under `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/<wave>/`; `pin.dispatch-evidence` in `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` |
