628:
629:Named legacy gaps (not claimed): the original seven gates do not ship the
630:§Gate standard digest-checked frozen-snapshot replayer. Round 38 supplies that
631:evidence for `anchor-truth` under `.ufo/waves/round-38/frozen/`: `expected.json`
632:pins the measured commit, input digests, source-blob digests, exit and verdict;
633:`replay.py.txt` checks every digest before launching the isolated replay.
634:Verdicts name the upstream source revision; cite the measured lane commit beside them.
635:Where this lane learns, and how far each source is trusted: `corpus/SOURCES.md`;
636:what a corpus entry must clear before admission: `corpus/QUALITY.md`.
637:
638:Error pattern — a floor keyed on a field the edit can rewrite (round 39, `corpus/QUALITY.md`
639:Q19). Symptom: `anchor-truth --base` reads CLEAN while an anchor that was true at the base is
640:now unchecked, false or moved, and the per-note totals still pass because another anchor was
641:repaired or a true copy was inserted. Cause: the round-38 floor fou
nd base entries by pin key,
642:and the key is built from the paired token (`corpus/lessons/round-38-verifier-spotcheck.md`,
643:R38-1). Decision since round 39: the `--base` comparison matches by raw text, resolved path and
644:occurrence index and counts non-true anchors per base-true raw text and path (`BASE_TRUE_LOST`);
645:the per-note check refuses a `pair` token that differs from the note's own pairing
646:(`TOKEN_FORGED`) and any entry source other than `pair` or `review:<seat>` with a token
647:(`PIN_INVALID`, exit 2). Fixtures AT23–AT27. Under the floor a base-true anchor's coordinates
648:are fixed: narrowing or moving one needs a new base, chosen in a round that records why.
649:Open limits: `review:<seat>` is self-declared in the pin (no committed review record is
650:required), and new false anchors at raw text that held no true anchor are accepted up to the
651:note's debt headroom against the frozen base (base debt minus current debt; 73 in the S8 note,
652:measured by a non-author seat in round 39), not only as a one-for-one trade. A swap of two
653:raw coordinates on one path can also move a base-true claim onto a false line while another
654:true anchor takes over its identity (L3), and a self-declared review with a stopword token can
655:forge a debt entry true (`corpus/lessons/round-39.md`, open limits and residual check).
656:
657:Error pattern — a floor that trusts what the judged change can write (round 40; builds on
658:round 39's Q19, `corpus/QUALITY.md`). Symptom: `anchor-truth --base` reads CLEAN while a pin entry
659:claims `review:<seat>` that no review ever made, while a base-true claim moved to another line
660:of the same file, or while new false anchors sit under the note's debt headroom against the
661:frozen base. Cause: review sources were self-declared, and the frozen base is too old to see
662:anchors repaired since (`corpus/lessons/round-39-verifier-spotcheck.md`, R39-1 to R39-3).
663:Decision since round 40: pass the round-open revision as `--open REV` (from the command line,
664:never from a lane file). A review source then needs a record committed at REV (`.ufo/waves/<round>/anchor-reviews.json`) that
665:names the same note, seat and token for the same anchor identity, or for a nested re-citation
666:only once that record's own anchor is gone (`REVIEW_UNBOUND`), and the pin at REV is
667:a second floor: `BASE_TRUE_LOST`, `DEBT_GREW`, `CHECKED_SHRANK` against it, and every debt
668:anchor must equal a debt anchor at REV by identity and token (`DEBT_NEW`). Fixtures AT31–AT34,
669:AT39–AT42; AT43–AT45 pin three round-39 survivors. Measure with
670:`node --input-type=module - --lane <lane> --rev <rev> --src <pin clone> --base <frozen base> < .ufo/waves/round-40/probe/floor-probe-v2.mjs.txt`
671:(26 attacks, 10 benign edits). Without
672:`--open` the gate reads records at HEAD and prints one `TRUTH_WARN` line, and the open-pin floor
673:does not run (the checklist item stays in this form so honest edits read as they did at round
674:open; the sound check passes `--open` explicitly). Open limits: under `--open`, narrowing or
675:widening a range true at REV is refused — the honest path is to keep that citation and add the
676:new one as a further anchor; no token-kept arm (`corpus/lessons/round-40.md`).
677:
678:## Verifiable checklist
679:
680:Twenty-six items (round 56; item 26 is the SOURCES duplicate-URL ratchet; item 25 is the opened-source byte-persistence gate; item 24 is the frozen-counter registry gate; item 23 remains the receipt-attest hermetic suite). Item 14 replaces the round-36/37 adjacency-fidelity
681:ratchet with the per-anchor truth gate on four registered notes (811 anchors);
682:item 15 is its hermetic suite; items 16–17 (round 41) are the wave-census of round 40's
683:committed swarm evidence (a fixed, landed round) and its hermetic suite; items 18–19 (round 42)
684:are the gate-mutants battery over the lane's own suites and its hermetic suite. Every item is read-only, runs from this repo's
685:root, and prints its verdict; `node scripts/surface-probe.mjs --checklists`
686:executes the list. The old `claims-check --fidelity` arm remains diagnostic for
687:its 20-note population, not a certificate of anchor truth.
688:
689:Items 3, 8, 10 and 14 are pin-aware — each resolves `--src` through
690:`.ufo/pins/origin.json` (contract `kumitate-origin-pin-v1`, a private clone
691:detached at a pinned revision) and prints `src-rev=<12 hex>` inside its verdict,
692:so a pass is scoreable against a revision instead of against whichever tree sits
693:at the default path. Item 1 (`cite-check`) still takes an explicit `--src`.
694:Unlike the legacy gates, item 14 fails closed without its origin pin.
695:
696:- [ ] Citation gate verdict — `node scripts/cite-check.mjs` → exit 0|1 + `CITE_CHECK:`
697:- [ ] Citation gate hermetic suite — `node scripts/cite-check.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
698:- [ ] Live sighting-surface conformance — `node scripts/surface-probe.mjs --known .ufo/pins/surface-known.json` → exit 0 + `SURFACE_PROBE: CLEAN`
699:- [ ] Surface-probe hermetic suite — `node scripts/surface-probe.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
700:- [ ] Round-gate hermetic suite — `node scripts/round-gate.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
701:- [ ] Round-close artifact audit — `node scripts/round-gate.mjs` → exit 0 + `ROUND_GATE: CLEAN`
702:- [ ] Filed-report tracking — `node scripts/round-gate.mjs --tracked` → exit 0 + `ROUND_GATE: CLEAN`
703:- [ ] Proxy recompute (`--strict` since round 42: a missing or renamed `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` block re-raises `PIN_UNPINNED`, which strict mode fails) — `node scripts/proxy-check.mjs --strict` → exit 0 + `PROXY: MATCH`
704:- [ ] Proxy-check hermetic suite — `node scripts/proxy-check.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
705:- [ ] Member-claims gate — `node scripts/claims-check.mjs` → exit 0 + `CLAIMS: MATCH`
706:- [ ] Kimi-substrate census — `node scripts/kimi-census.mjs` → exit 0 + `KIMI_CENSUS: CLEAN`
707:- [ ] Sources-registry gate — `node scripts/sources-check.mjs` → exit 0 + `SOURCES_CHECK: CLEAN`
708:- [ ] Sources-check hermetic suite — `node scripts/sources-check.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
709:- [ ] Per-anchor truth burn-down — `node scripts/anchor-truth.mjs --base e18ff1af3392e3823227644c977c237737fe65c9` → exit 0 + `TRUTH: CLEAN`
710:- [ ] Anchor-truth hermetic suite — `node scripts/anchor-truth.mjs --selftest` → exit 0 + `VERDICT: PASS`
