726:
727:
728:Exit 2, or no verdict line at all, is a tool/environment fault (`--src` missing,
729:empty scan set, unparsable surface JSON, a pin that no longer resolves to its
730:recorded revision, a ratchet whose revision is stale): fix the tool, not the
731:claim. A named `CITE_CHECK: DRIFT` / `SURFACE_PROBE: DRIFT` is a tree finding —
732:the gate measured the tree, the owner named in that line owns the repair. With a
733:pin active (`.ufo/pins/origin.json`, contract `kumitate-origin-pin-v1`) the
734:pin-aware gates resolve `--src` from the pin's read-only clone, assert
735:that clone's `HEAD` equals the pinned revision, and print `src-rev=<12 hex>`
736:inside the verdict line, so a clean verdict is a statement about a revision and
737:not about whichever tree happens to sit at the default path; the probe's origin
738:read verbs run with `UFO_STATE_DIR` / `UFO_PENDING_WORK_PATH` under a `mkdtemp`
739:and the temp dir is removed afterwards, so no gate writes into the tree it
740:reads. Without a pin file the gates behave as before and the verdict carries no
741:`src-rev=` segment. The counts below are a dated snapshot, not a live claim —
742:re-run the item and read the line it prints. At round-13 close (2026-09-28):
743:`CITE_CHECK: DRIFT (files=47 tokens=4530 errors=14 warnings=75)` — every error
744:sits inside third-party aggregator artifacts
745:(`corpus/lessons/round-6-aggregator-audit.md` 2 × `LINE_OOR`;
746:`corpus/lessons/round-8-aggregator-box3-coldrun.md` 12, that file being extended
747:by its owner during the round), and **zero are in this lane's own prose**. The
748:third-party count is not stable — it moved 7 → 14 inside one round as the
749:auditor's artifact grew — so the durable claim is the lane-local one: no lane
750:document may appear in that list. One consequence, paid for in round 11: a **bare sha of a superseded
751:revision** in a corpus doc is read as a content pin of the nearest cited file and
752:becomes a `PIN_MISMATCH` error the moment that file changes, so superseded
753:revisions are described, not pinned — only the current revision's sha appears in
754:a `.md`, and the historical ones live in `LOG.md`.
755:
756:Round 16 gives the retired `coverage` axis's two successors their first measured
757:terms inside the same `kumitate-proxy-v1` verdict. `coverage:script-layer` =
758:`floor(10 × C1s/C1s_total × S_sections/S_members)` over the registry rows whose
759:id starts `S`; `coverage:runtime-layer` = `floor(10 × C1r/C1r_total ×
760:R_sections/R_members)` over the `R` rows. `C1s`/`C1r` are each layer's `yes`
761:rows over that layer's registry rows; the sections term is the Σ of member
762:sections the claims gate verifies in those rows' notes, **in-family only** (a
763:section the gate grades `SECTION_FILE_NOT_MEMBER` — R9's 3 sibling-suite
764:sections — is excluded, so current `R_sections` is 69 of the 72 raw runtime-row
765:sections; round 16 first measured 60 of 63); the member term is the layer's
766:declared members counted from the origin tree — script layer `scripts/*.mjs`
767:(72) + every file under `scripts/*/` (42, recursive: a depth-1 count reads 38
768:and is wrong), runtime layer `crates/ufo-core-runtime/src/*.rs` (93) +
769:`crates/ufo-cli/src/*.rs` (5). Current 2026-09-29 measurement:
770:`8/8 × 74/114` ⇒ **6** and `11/11 × 69/98` ⇒ **7**, against the retired
771:parent's terminal 10 (round 16's first reading was 6/6 at runtime 60/98).
772:The stanza therefore carries six more integer terms — `S_members`,
773:`S_sections`, `R_members`, `R_sections`, `coverage_script`,
774:`coverage_runtime` (the stanza's `key=value` charset forbids `:`, so the axis
775:name `coverage:script-layer` is carried by the key `coverage_script`).
776:Amendment to the proxy's self-only invariant: the legacy terms (`A`, `C`,
777:`C1`/`C1_total`, `C2`/`C2_total` and the scores derived from them) still read
778:this repo alone, while the four layer terms read the origin tree **once**,
779:in-process — `proxy-check` imports `probeSections` from
780:`scripts/claims-check.mjs` (one walk, no subprocess, no second traversal) — so
781:the `Proxy recompute` item now needs the origin tree exactly as `cite-check`,
782:`claims-check` and `surface-probe` already do: `--src DIR` is accepted
783:(`$UFO_SRC` or the ufo-fsd-alpha tree by default), and a `--src` that is not a
784:directory is the new fail-closed arm `SRC_NOT_A_DIR` (exit 2), never a scored
785:zero — the layer terms cannot be computed without the tree.
786:
787:`ROUND_GATE: DRIFT` is this lane's own record, and the kinds in that line name
788:what is missing (a thin report, a missing `SCORECARD.md` row or `LOG.md` entry,
789:no `round-<N>` commit marker, a cited commit that does not resolve or is no
790:longer an ancestor of lane `HEAD`) — the repair is this lane's, not another
791:lane's. Warnings (`SCORECARD_PLAN_MISSING`, `REPORT_SHONEN_MISSING`) print but do
792:not gate unless `--strict`; kinds, thresholds and the boundary against the
793:integrator's fleet-conformance step are in
794:`corpus/knowledge/round-close-gate.md`.
795:
796:## Working rules for this repo
797:
798:- Re-verify before claiming: `node scripts/cite-check.mjs` (repo-local,
799:  read-only, zero deps, node ≥20) re-resolves every path / line / symbol / pin
800:  in `SKILL.md` + `corpus/**/*.md` against the origin tree and prints
801:  `CITE_CHECK: CLEAN|DRIFT (…)` — exit 0 clean, 1 on source-class findings, 2
802:  fail-closed (missing `--src`, empty scan set). `--selftest` runs the hermetic
803:  20-case fixture suite (fixtures only — live-tree assertions moved to
804:  `--integrations`, which is where a sibling lane's doc drift shows up);
805:  `--json` is the machine interface. Bounds: workspace/run artifacts (`.ufo/…`,
806:  `manifest.json`, …), HOME config candidates and `$OUT_DIR`-generated files are
807:  informational by construction — they cannot be verified from the source tree;
808:  `--strict` promotes warnings to failure.
809:- Re-verify the live surfaces the same way: `node scripts/surface-probe.mjs`
810:  (contract `kumitate-surface-probe-v1`) re-derives the `ufo-sighting surface
811:  --json` manifest and the `fleet-dispatcher.mjs status` projection against the
812:  origin bytes, then reports `SURFACE_PROBE: CLEAN|DRIFT (…)`; `--selftest` is
813:  hermetic, `--checklists` runs the checklist above. Two digests, one pin: the
814:  pin `config/ufo.json` `sighting.surfaceDigest` hashes `canonicalJson(manifest)`
815:  (`sync-ufo-contracts.mjs:853-862`), while `manifest.scriptDigest` hashes
816:  concatenated file bytes (`ufo-sighting-lib/surface.mjs:43-60`) — comparing the
817:  pin to `scriptDigest` is always a false drift signal.
818:- Re-verify the registry's own claim: `node scripts/claims-check.mjs` (contract
819:  `kumitate-claims-v1`) re-derives every `yes` cell from the corpus note behind it
820:  — note resolution, one member section per file with a live own-file anchor and a
821:  verbatim symbol, and the declared member count when the cell names one. Live
822:  2026-09-29: `CLAIMS: MATCH (rows=19 yes=19 notes=27 sections=146 adv=14)`
823:  exit 0; the 14 advisories are the family standard's printed residue (8
824:  topic-form rows, 3 count-suspect rows, R9's 3 sibling-suite sections) and
825:  `--strict` promotes them to exit 1. For a row that changes a layer score,
826:  additionally require row-local adv=0 and prove section occurrences equal
827:  distinct resolved in-family files: until round 35 `proxy-check` counted
828:  occurrences while the gate dedupes only for declared-count findings
829:  (`SCORECARD.md` round-17 limit). It is the compensating check for the
830:  scorecard arithmetic's historical note-blind spot; contract, arms, anchor
831:  semantics and limits:
832:  `corpus/knowledge/member-claims-gate.md`.
833:  *Round 35 (2026-10-20):* `proxy-check` now derives `S_sections`/`R_sections`
834:  as DISTINCT in-family member identities (`section.file`), so the
835:  duplicate-one/drop-one note mutation fires `S_SECTIONS_DRIFT`/
836:  `R_SECTIONS_DRIFT` (hermetic cases 15–19); the claims gate's printed
837:  `sections=` total is still a raw occurrence count, not the proxy term.
838:- Re-verify the round-close contract before claiming a round done:
839:  `node scripts/round-gate.mjs` (contract `kumitate-round-gate-v1`; kinds,
840:  thresholds, fail-closed arms and the boundary against the integrator's
841:  fleet-conformance step in `corpus/knowledge/round-close-gate.md`) audits THIS
842:  lane's own round artifacts — a tripwire + integration smoke, not a guarantee:
843:  a round that filed no report at all is invisible to it (`--round N` audits one
844:  by hand). Unflagged it audits the latest closed round = max N with
845:  `<reports-dir>/round-<N>/<lane>.md` present (none ⇒ fail-closed 2; `--lane`
846:  defaults to `kumitate`, `--reports-dir` to `<lane repo>/../.ufo/reports` —
847:  derived from `resolve(HERE, '..', '..')`, the lane repo's parent, so the
848:  default follows a moved checkout (the repo's 2026-09-29 move to
849:  `~/Projects` broke the old literal `/home/vgpnk/projects/...` default;
850:  env/flag overrides unchanged). It re-derives, never re-runs:
851:  report presence / weight / headings / round identity / `SHONEN` heading, cited
852:  commit tokens resolving and staying ancestors of lane `HEAD`
853:  (`PROTOCOL.md:264-265`), a `SCORECARD.md` row, a `LOG.md` entry, a
854:  `round-<N>` commit marker. `--close` adds the close-only trio (clean tree,
855:  nothing unpushed, report tracked + pushed in `--main-repo`) — deliberately not
856:  a checklist item, since it is red until the round is committed and pushed.
857:  `--tracked` is the mid-round shadow of that trio's tracking clause and runs NO
858:  audit check of its own: it enumerates `<reports-dir>/round-*/<lane>.md`, drops
859:  the highest round (the in-flight one), and requires every older report to be
860:  tracked in `--main-repo` — each miss is `REPORT_UNTRACKED`. Fewer than two
861:  filed reports ⇒ fail-closed 2 `NO_FILED_REPORTS` (nothing older can be
862:  checked, so the mode refuses rather than reporting CLEAN); `--tracked` with
863:  `--close` is usage 64 (mutually exclusive modes). Verdict text is
864:  `ROUND_GATE: CLEAN|DRIFT (mode=tracked checked=<n> errors=<e> warnings=<w>)`.
865:  Exit 0 clean · 1 findings · 2 fail-closed · 64 usage; `--json` is the machine
866:  interface, `--selftest` the hermetic suite.
867:- Keep the measurement itself honest: `node scripts/proxy-check.mjs` (contract
868:  `kumitate-proxy-v1`, zero deps, node ≥20, READ-ONLY, no network) recomputes
869:  the frozen proxy terms from the tree — A (count of `*.mjs|*.js|*.sh|*.py`
870:  files), C (`SKILL.md` lines matching `/^\s*- \[/`), C1/C1_total (registry rows
871:  whose 4th cell starts `yes`, over all registry rows), C2/C2_total (`README.md`
872:  note rows over corpus note files) — plus the four layer terms it reads from
873:  the origin tree: the script layer is `scripts/*.mjs` (72) + every file under
874:  `scripts/*/` (42, recursive — a depth-1 count reads 38), the runtime layer is
875:  `crates/ufo-core-runtime/src/*.rs` (93) + `crates/ufo-cli/src/*.rs` (5), and
876:  `S_sections`/`R_sections` are the member sections the claims gate verifies in
877:  those rows' notes — `inFamily` sections only, so R9's 3 sibling-suite sections
878:  are excluded and the readout is 74 / 60 (63 raw; the excluded three belong to
879:  R2/R6/R7) — and it then derives four scores
880:  (`floor(10×(A+C)/(A+C+3))`, `floor(10×(C1/C1_total)×(C2/C2_total))`,
881:  `coverage_script = floor(10×(C1s/C1s_total)×(S_sections/S_members))` = 6,
882:  `coverage_runtime = floor(10×(C1r/C1r_total)×(R_sections/R_members))` = 6,
883:  `C1s`/`C1r` being each layer's `yes` rows over that layer's registry rows —
884:  the two successors of the retired
885:  `coverage` axis, first measured 2026-09-28) and compares them against the
886:  `## Axes` table, whose rows now include `coverage:script-layer` and
887:  `coverage:runtime-layer`, plus the five `scripts/*.mjs` sha256 pins. The claim
888:  block it reads is one HTML comment in `SCORECARD.md`
889:  whose first line is `<!-- kumitate-proxy-v1`, body lines `key=value` (`A`,
890:  `C`, `C1`, `C1_total`, `C2`, `C2_total`, `S_members`, `S_sections`,
891:  `R_members`, `R_sections`, `coverage_script`, `coverage_runtime`,
892:  `pin.cite-check`, `pin.surface-probe`,
893:  `pin.round-gate`, `pin.proxy-check`, `pin.claims-check`): `PROXY: MATCH (…)` exit 0,
894:  `PROXY: DRIFT (…)` exit 1 naming each term delta, 2 fail-closed
895:  (`SCORECARD_MISSING`, `STANZA_MISSING`, `STANZA_MALFORMED`,
896:  `STANZA_KEY_UNKNOWN`, `STANZA_KEY_DUPLICATE`, `REGISTRY_MISSING`,
897:  `SKILL_MISSING`, `README_MISSING`, `CORPUS_DIRS_MISSING`, `SELF_NOT_A_DIR`,
898:  and `SRC_NOT_A_DIR` when `--src` is not a directory),
899:  64 usage. Because the stanza carries `pin.proxy-check`, ANY later edit to the
900:  tool must re-pin or the live run reports `PIN_DRIFT` — intended, not a wart.
901:  What it does NOT do: it recomputes claims, it cannot show that a claim is
902:  well-founded (a registry row flipped to `yes` with no note behind it still
903:  passes — the note's own citations are `cite-check`'s job), and the file-level
904:  residue diagnostic (origin-tree basenames) is not covered. Amendment (round
905:  16): the legacy terms (`A`, `C`, `C1`/`C1_total`, `C2`/`C2_total` and the
906:  `operability`/`coverage` scores derived from them) stay self-only, but the
907:  layer terms read the origin
908:  tree once and in-process, never via a subprocess — the tool imports
909:  `probeSections` from `scripts/claims-check.mjs` and consumes the single walk
910:  that gate already performs, so a missing or non-directory `--src` is
911:  `SRC_NOT_A_DIR`, not a scored zero. It is portable: any lane that writes the
912:  same block into its own `SCORECARD.md` can be re-derived by a non-author with
913:  `--self <lane repo>`; the layer terms additionally need `--src`.
914:- Cite file + symbol for every claim; if the source moves, update the
915:  citation, not the claim from memory.
916:- Constants live once: `ENTRY_FAILURE_CLASSES`, `CAPACITY_FAILURES`,
917:  `PROPOSAL_ROLES`, deadline/seat-class maps — import or quote the source,
918:  never a restated copy.
919:- OMP lane vocabulary: spawn lane = `tasks[]` entry; resume lane =
920:  `write agent://<id>`; member name `[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]{1,31}`; run id
921:  `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,15}` at the native launcher.
